    {
      "title": "Houthi attack kills 53 in biggest single loss of life since Yemen civil war reignited",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/houthi-attack-yemen-al-alam-camp-biggest-single-loss-of-life-civil-war",
      "description": "<p>More than 200 mostly young people said to be injured after ballistic missile attack on training camp for government forces </p><p>At least 53 people have been killed in a Houthi ballistic missile attack on a training camp for Yemeni government security forces, making it the largest single loss of life since the country’s civil war reignited in September.</p><p>The attack on al-Alam camp in the southern Shabwa province was said to have injured more than 200 others, mostly young recruits, and was described as a disaster by the country’s UN-recognised government. The injured were taken from the police and army training camp in the Jardan district to a hospital in the local capital, Ataq, where pleas for blood donations were made.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/houthi-attack-yemen-al-alam-camp-biggest-single-loss-of-life-civil-war\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-19T17:15:23"
    },
    {
      "title": "Houthi Strikes Kill Dozens in Yemeni Desert Military Camp, Officials Say",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/19/world/middleeast/houthis-strike-yemen-military-camp.html",
      "description": "The Iranian-backed militia struck with ballistic missiles deep in government-held central Yemen, in what appeared to be among the deadliest attacks of the renewed war.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-19T19:54:36"
